   "heard": "UPSC, twenty nineteen. General Studies Paper Two, fifteen marks, two hundred and fifty words. Can Parliament destroy the Constitution's basic structure by expanding its own amending power? Here's the strange part. Parliament once wrote a clause that tried to do exactly that."
